PARITY NOTES (web -> native; web is THE spec)
  • Data: web reads `useVehicles` (selected vehicle) + a live `VehicleState` +
    `useWakeVehicle`; native binds the same three via the P1/S8 `VehicleHeaderSource`
    seam (production wraps the shared holders) — no HTTP in the view.
  • Status: web `status = vehicle ? deriveVehicleStatus(state) : 'offline'` and the
    `deriveVehicleStatus` ladder (charging > speed>0 driving > lowercased FSM state >
    online; nil -> offline) ported verbatim into `VehicleStatus.derive` + unit-asserted.
  • Title: `display_name || vin || t('common.vehicle','Vehicle')` (the web key reused) —
    JS-empty-string falsiness reproduced (each candidate must be non-empty) + asserted.
  • Subtitle: `${model} ${trim_badging} · ${vin}` — model/trim words joined (empties
    dropped), middot-separated VIN rendered monospaced (web `font-mono`) + asserted.
  • StatusBadge: web resolves a per-state dot tint from the FSM `VEHICLE_STATE_ENTRIES`
    variant (online=success, charging=warning, parked/updating=info, asleep=neutral,
    offline=danger; driving shares `success`). The web `badgeDot` overrides (blue/cyan/
    indigo/purple) are decorative Tailwind tints; native maps each status to its semantic
    variant tone from the design tokens (ADR-009), so light/dark/high-contrast stay
    correct. Documented in code, NOT silent drift.
  • Wake: web `<Button loading={isPending} icon={<Power/>}>` -> a `TSButton` primary with
    the `power` SF Symbol; `loading` driven by the bound wake lifecycle. The web
    `onSuccess: () => setTimeout(() => onRefetchState(), 5000)` is reproduced as the
    model's wake-success edge -> a single delayed `refresh()` via an injected scheduler,
    unit-tested (delay value + one-shot-per-cycle + failure-does-not-schedule).
  • Navigation: web `<Link to="/vehicles">`. Surfaced as the `onBack` closure (the host
    maps it); the view never navigates itself.
  • States: the web component itself only renders content (its parent owns load/error).
    The Apple leaf contract requires every state to render, so the surface adds
    loading (skeleton) / empty (no-vehicle, never blank) / error+retry, plus the
    orthogonal stale + offline freshness chip with a one-shot stale auto-refresh — all
    bound through the model, all rendered (never a hidden surface).
  • Charts/maps: NONE in the web source — nothing to port to Swift Charts / MapKit.

